# Ignore rules for this repository.
#
# The first entry is the important one: `local_secrets.py` holds a real API key so
# it does not have to be exported before every run, and a key in a tracked file is a
# key burned the first time this repository is pushed anywhere.

# --- credentials -------------------------------------------------------------
wilcom_pipeline/local_secrets.py
*.env
.env

# --- python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# Every virtualenv name in common use. `.venv/` alone is not enough: a checkout
# that was set up with `python -m venv env` or a tool-created `.env` directory
# would otherwise commit 500 MB of interpreter. `pip install -r
# wilcom_pipeline/requirements.txt` is the source of truth -- never the tree.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.env/

.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
build/
dist/

# --- node --------------------------------------------------------------------
# `node_modules/` matches at any depth, so the list below is redundant but kept
# as documentation of where the trees actually live. `frontend/package.json` and
# `frontend/package-lock.json` are the source of truth: run `npm install`.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
frontend/.vite/

# --- pipeline output ---------------------------------------------------------
# Generated, large, and fully regenerable from the URLs in `wilcom_work/screening`.
# Each work tree holds clips, frames and cached model replies, which are tens of
# megabytes of things that can be rebuilt.
#
# `wilcom_medium/` and `wilcom_medium_src/` are the same kind of tree as
# `wilcom_work/`: local scratch output from one tutorial (a ~28 MB source video,
# its clips, cached model replies and the extracted trajectory), left over from
# trying a second quality preset. Nothing here is an input to the code, and the
# video is re-downloadable, so it does not belong in the repository.
wilcom_work/
wilcom_work_*/
wilcom_medium/
wilcom_medium_src/

# --- editor ------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# --- reference papers --------------------------------------------------------
# The WILCOM paper was committed as a Git LFS pointer in the initial pipeline
# commit, but it is a document to read, not an artifact the code consumes. It is
# re-downloadable, so it is untracked here: keep it on disk, out of the repo.
# Ignored by exact name so `2605.14747v1.pdf_by_PaddleOCR-VL-1.6.md`, which IS
# tracked, still matches no rule.
2605.14747v1.pdf
